  ('0e76719d-5eea-4ff9-9f30-87f737f6f648'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000308'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99341', 'telehealth_allowed', '{"answer":"Telehealth delivery is permitted, but conditionally: if a member has been receiving services by telehealth for more than 12 consecutive months, the practice must conduct at least one in-person annual visit, or refer the member to a practitioner or their usual source of clinical care (not an emergency department) for an in-person annual visit. For a home-based palliative panel seen mostly virtually, schedule and document one in-person visit per 12 months. Stated by service, so it governs telehealth-delivered home/domiciliary E/M (99341-99350), ACP (99497, 99498), prolonged services (99417, G0318), TCM (99495, 99496) and CCM/PCM (99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427).","appliesToService":"Telehealth services provided by your office (telemedicine services are listed as a covered service)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'covered', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f85ab415-9c8e-4dab-a085-35ba7a0a620d'::uuid, 'If telehealth services are rendered to a member for a period longer than 12 consecutive months, providers are expected to conduct at least one in-person annual visit or refer the member to a practitioner or their usual source of clinical care that is not an emergency department for an in-person annual visit.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
