  ('0a71c721-7abe-4240-a3eb-188ed8afc171'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000201'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99439', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Add-on codes must never appear without their primary/base code on the claim, and if the base code is denied the add-on is denied automatically. Bill prolonged service 99417 or G0318 only with its base home-visit E/M; 99498 only with 99497; 99439 only with 99490; 99425 only with 99424; 99427 only with 99426. The editor also flags a base code billed in a quantity greater than one where an add-on should have been used — bill one unit of the base plus the correct add-on units instead.","appliesToService":"Add-on and Base Code Edits (Code Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, '77290c16-75fd-42b6-8200-f5fa87d64525'::uuid, 'These code editing rules look for claims in which the add-on CPT code was billed without the primary service CPT code. If the primary service code is denied, then the add-on code is also denied.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
