  ('1adea2e0-50b5-42e6-92b1-e5570eda0540'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000203'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"NPs and PAs may bill Healthy Blue only if they are credentialed, and Healthy Blue will not credential an NP or PA who is not under the direct supervision of a doctor - the supervising physician must himself/herself be credentialed with Healthy Blue and active in their systems before the NP/PA can be enrolled. Once credentialed, the NP/PA must bill under their OWN individual NPI (rendering NPI in box 24J), not under the supervising physician''s NPI. Billing an NP/PA home visit under the physician''s NPI, or billing before the NP/PA''s own credentialing is complete, is a denial. Effective dates are not retroactive - do not see patients before the welcome email network effective date.","appliesToService":"\"Certifying Advanced Practice Practitioners\" - physician assistants (PAs) and nurse practitioners (NPs) enrolling and billing for services. Governs who may render and bill the home-visit, advance care planning, home health oversight, transitional care and care management services a palliative practice delivers.","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'covered', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, '05460b0d-4e8b-4d5f-a991-ce1a69654967'::uuid, 'If the PA or NP is approved and credentialed with Healthy Blue, he or she should bill for services under his or her individual NPI.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
