  ('4bcbd22b-6fff-46dc-a511-25c436eeed09'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000102'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99427', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"The plan enforces a maximum daily frequency per procedure code; the manual does not publish the per-code values. If a service must exceed that daily frequency — for example more than one home visit or more than the standard units of a timed service on the same date — submit the medical records justifying medical necessity, otherwise the excess line denies. Build this into the claim workflow rather than waiting for the denial and reconsideration.","appliesToService":"the maximum daily frequency for a procedure","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, '368783d1-c669-4007-9476-92a53ea6ae06'::uuid, 'If you must exceed the maximum daily frequency for a procedure, submit the medical records justifying medical necessity', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('ef9eaa73-bde1-412f-95a9-f4f6e5b15fc1'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Do not expect separate payment for a home/house-call E/M visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345, 99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) that falls 1 day before, on the same date as, or within the 90-day post-operative period of a major surgical procedure - CCH''s code auditing bundles it into the global surgical package and the E/M line is denied. If the home visit is genuinely unrelated to the surgery, it must be supported by a modifier (e.g. -24) and documentation, since clinical validation reviews these lines.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period)\" reported 1 day preoperatively, on the same date of service, or during the 90-day post-operative period (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period) that are reported 1- day preoperatively, on the same date of service or during the 90-day post-operative period are not recommended for separate reimbursement.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('35680b94-bfeb-4244-84f9-c5e2b4b1c17a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Do not expect separate payment for a home/house-call E/M visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345, 99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) that falls 1 day before, on the same date as, or within the 90-day post-operative period of a major surgical procedure - CCH''s code auditing bundles it into the global surgical package and the E/M line is denied. If the home visit is genuinely unrelated to the surgery, it must be supported by a modifier (e.g. -24) and documentation, since clinical validation reviews these lines.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period)\" reported 1 day preoperatively, on the same date of service, or during the 90-day post-operative period (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period) that are reported 1- day preoperatively, on the same date of service or during the 90-day post-operative period are not recommended for separate reimbursement.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('c06d1d97-5ece-4abe-99ce-2d3afff95c54'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99344', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Do not expect separate payment for a home/house-call E/M visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345, 99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) that falls 1 day before, on the same date as, or within the 90-day post-operative period of a major surgical procedure - CCH''s code auditing bundles it into the global surgical package and the E/M line is denied. If the home visit is genuinely unrelated to the surgery, it must be supported by a modifier (e.g. -24) and documentation, since clinical validation reviews these lines.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period)\" reported 1 day preoperatively, on the same date of service, or during the 90-day post-operative period (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period) that are reported 1- day preoperatively, on the same date of service or during the 90-day post-operative period are not recommended for separate reimbursement.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('bc2c1269-4cc0-4a01-8b67-087637e7ee61'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99345', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Do not expect separate payment for a home/house-call E/M visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345, 99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) that falls 1 day before, on the same date as, or within the 90-day post-operative period of a major surgical procedure - CCH''s code auditing bundles it into the global surgical package and the E/M line is denied. If the home visit is genuinely unrelated to the surgery, it must be supported by a modifier (e.g. -24) and documentation, since clinical validation reviews these lines.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period)\" reported 1 day preoperatively, on the same date of service, or during the 90-day post-operative period (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for a major procedure (90-day period) that are reported 1- day preoperatively, on the same date of service or during the 90-day post-operative period are not recommended for separate reimbursement.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('ca892483-5519-412f-adce-e8060adbae0c'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99347', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"For an ESTABLISHED patient home visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) billed on the same day as a 0-day-global procedure, the E/M is treated as inherent to the procedure and is not reimbursed. This is the most common bundling trap for home-based practices that perform a small procedure at the same encounter - bill the E/M only when a significant, separately identifiable service is documented and modifier 25 is used.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period\" on the same day of surgery (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period are not recommended for reimbursement on the same day of surgery because there is an inherent evaluation and management service included in all surgical procedures.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('39aa5631-193a-4573-9538-bf578035134f'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99348', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"For an ESTABLISHED patient home visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) billed on the same day as a 0-day-global procedure, the E/M is treated as inherent to the procedure and is not reimbursed. This is the most common bundling trap for home-based practices that perform a small procedure at the same encounter - bill the E/M only when a significant, separately identifiable service is documented and modifier 25 is used.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period\" on the same day of surgery (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period are not recommended for reimbursement on the same day of surgery because there is an inherent evaluation and management service included in all surgical procedures.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('42132d6d-2e77-4bfb-a004-2adac913ab53'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99349', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"For an ESTABLISHED patient home visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) billed on the same day as a 0-day-global procedure, the E/M is treated as inherent to the procedure and is not reimbursed. This is the most common bundling trap for home-based practices that perform a small procedure at the same encounter - bill the E/M only when a significant, separately identifiable service is documented and modifier 25 is used.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period\" on the same day of surgery (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period are not recommended for reimbursement on the same day of surgery because there is an inherent evaluation and management service included in all surgical procedures.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('4e632e77-3f91-48dd-a86e-9432f946639e'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99350', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"For an ESTABLISHED patient home visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) billed on the same day as a 0-day-global procedure, the E/M is treated as inherent to the procedure and is not reimbursed. This is the most common bundling trap for home-based practices that perform a small procedure at the same encounter - bill the E/M only when a significant, separately identifiable service is documented and modifier 25 is used.","appliesToService":"\"Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period\" on the same day of surgery (Global Surgical Period Editing/Medical Visit Editing)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Evaluation and Management services for established patients that are reported with surgical procedures that have a 0-day global surgical period are not recommended for reimbursement on the same day of surgery because there is an inherent evaluation and management service included in all surgical procedures.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('92158af0-9a4c-4ba4-98aa-bfd60db33dfa'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"Only one CPT/HCPCS code and up to four modifiers per claim line, and only the FIRST modifier is used to price the line - so the pricing modifier (e.g. 25 on a home-visit E/M, or 59/X{EPSU}) must be in the first position, ahead of informational modifiers. Wrong modifier position, an invalid modifier/code combination, or a code not valid for the date of service will get the line rejected, denied or paid incorrectly.","appliesToService":"Field 24 D (unshaded) of the CMS-1500, \"PROCEDURES, SERVICES OR SUPPLIES CPT/HCPCS MODIFIER\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Only the first modifier entered is used for pricing the claim. Failure to use modifiers in the correct position or combination with the Procedure Code, or invalid use of modifiers, will result in a rejected, denied, or incorrectly paid claim.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('3a138a77-f0bf-46f2-a8e3-f9a28588750b'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"Only one CPT/HCPCS code and up to four modifiers per claim line, and only the FIRST modifier is used to price the line - so the pricing modifier (e.g. 25 on a home-visit E/M, or 59/X{EPSU}) must be in the first position, ahead of informational modifiers. Wrong modifier position, an invalid modifier/code combination, or a code not valid for the date of service will get the line rejected, denied or paid incorrectly.","appliesToService":"Field 24 D (unshaded) of the CMS-1500, \"PROCEDURES, SERVICES OR SUPPLIES CPT/HCPCS MODIFIER\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Only the first modifier entered is used for pricing the claim. Failure to use modifiers in the correct position or combination with the Procedure Code, or invalid use of modifiers, will result in a rejected, denied, or incorrectly paid claim.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
