  ('7ddb57a7-a58e-4eb3-9dcd-1fbfb9883c3a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99424', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Any of these codes will deny as unbundled when it is a component of a more comprehensive code billed for the same patient on the same date of service (CMS NCCI Column 1/Column 2 edits). Practical cases: ACP (99497/99498) or prolonged service (99417/G0318) billed alongside a code that already includes that work, or a home-visit E/M billed with a service that subsumes it. Check the code pair in CCH''s Code Editing Assistant on the secure provider portal before submitting.","appliesToService":"\"Code billed is a part of a more comprehensive code billed on same date of service\" - listed by CCH as a code-related reason a claim may reject or deny; enforced through CMS NCCI Column 1/Column II (PTP) unbundling edits","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Code billed is a part of a more comprehensive code billed on same date of service', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('59581689-de08-4b44-81fd-ee2e541c132c'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99426', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Any of these codes will deny as unbundled when it is a component of a more comprehensive code billed for the same patient on the same date of service (CMS NCCI Column 1/Column 2 edits). Practical cases: ACP (99497/99498) or prolonged service (99417/G0318) billed alongside a code that already includes that work, or a home-visit E/M billed with a service that subsumes it. Check the code pair in CCH''s Code Editing Assistant on the secure provider portal before submitting.","appliesToService":"\"Code billed is a part of a more comprehensive code billed on same date of service\" - listed by CCH as a code-related reason a claim may reject or deny; enforced through CMS NCCI Column 1/Column II (PTP) unbundling edits","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'Code billed is a part of a more comprehensive code billed on same date of service', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('71ffe88f-3be9-44e3-a356-689256f921aa'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Bill a NEW patient home visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345) only once per patient per provider per three years. If the same provider bills a new-patient E/M within three years of a previous new-patient visit, CCH denies that line and replaces it with the corresponding ESTABLISHED patient visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) - reimbursement drops to the established-patient rate. For any patient seen by the practice within the last three years, bill the established home-visit codes.","appliesToService":"\"a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit\" (Replacement Edits)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'the rule will evaluate if a provider has billed a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit. This rule will replace the second submission with the appropriate established patient visit.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('1e8098bf-c485-4261-a926-db44d63b2a3b'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Bill a NEW patient home visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345) only once per patient per provider per three years. If the same provider bills a new-patient E/M within three years of a previous new-patient visit, CCH denies that line and replaces it with the corresponding ESTABLISHED patient visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) - reimbursement drops to the established-patient rate. For any patient seen by the practice within the last three years, bill the established home-visit codes.","appliesToService":"\"a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit\" (Replacement Edits)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'the rule will evaluate if a provider has billed a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit. This rule will replace the second submission with the appropriate established patient visit.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('7f05d256-6af2-4f39-9b23-d342a1787e55'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99344', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Bill a NEW patient home visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345) only once per patient per provider per three years. If the same provider bills a new-patient E/M within three years of a previous new-patient visit, CCH denies that line and replaces it with the corresponding ESTABLISHED patient visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) - reimbursement drops to the established-patient rate. For any patient seen by the practice within the last three years, bill the established home-visit codes.","appliesToService":"\"a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit\" (Replacement Edits)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'the rule will evaluate if a provider has billed a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit. This rule will replace the second submission with the appropriate established patient visit.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('3a74fa92-8119-4b1c-8eef-c346453f1be4'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99345', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Bill a NEW patient home visit (99341, 99342, 99344, 99345) only once per patient per provider per three years. If the same provider bills a new-patient E/M within three years of a previous new-patient visit, CCH denies that line and replaces it with the corresponding ESTABLISHED patient visit (99347, 99348, 99349, 99350) - reimbursement drops to the established-patient rate. For any patient seen by the practice within the last three years, bill the established home-visit codes.","appliesToService":"\"a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit\" (Replacement Edits)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'the rule will evaluate if a provider has billed a new patient evaluation and management code within three years of a previous new patient visit. This rule will replace the second submission with the appropriate established patient visit.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('ec3a203a-126e-4cb7-b06c-ba482d6b3133'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99347', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Only one clinician may be paid for the same code, same patient, same date of service - CCH''s duplicate edits look across providers and across the practice''s history, not just within one claim. In a home-based palliative practice this bites when an NP and a physician each bill a home visit (99341-99350) for the same patient on the same day, or when two clinicians both bill ACP/care management for the same date. Coordinate so a single clinician bills the encounter, or expect the second line to deny as a duplicate.","appliesToService":"Duplicate Edits - the software looks \"across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service\"; the manual''s own example is \"a nurse practitioner and physician bill for office visits for the same enrollee on the same day\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'The software will also look across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
  ('cadbd30b-4ce2-49ac-83d8-0c9dcda4ef1a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99348', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Only one clinician may be paid for the same code, same patient, same date of service - CCH''s duplicate edits look across providers and across the practice''s history, not just within one claim. In a home-based palliative practice this bites when an NP and a physician each bill a home visit (99341-99350) for the same patient on the same day, or when two clinicians both bill ACP/care management for the same date. Coordinate so a single clinician bills the encounter, or expect the second line to deny as a duplicate.","appliesToService":"Duplicate Edits - the software looks \"across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service\"; the manual''s own example is \"a nurse practitioner and physician bill for office visits for the same enrollee on the same day\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'The software will also look across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
