  ('b612df02-c42b-4abf-a6ae-0de0ca3a4cbd'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000104'::uuid, 'NC', 'medicaid_mco', '99350', 'frequency_limit', '{"answer":"Only one clinician may be paid for the same code, same patient, same date of service - CCH''s duplicate edits look across providers and across the practice''s history, not just within one claim. In a home-based palliative practice this bites when an NP and a physician each bill a home visit (99341-99350) for the same patient on the same day, or when two clinicians both bill ACP/care management for the same date. Coordinate so a single clinician bills the encounter, or expect the second line to deny as a duplicate.","appliesToService":"Duplicate Edits - the software looks \"across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service\"; the manual''s own example is \"a nurse practitioner and physician bill for office visits for the same enrollee on the same day\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code"}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.80, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'cbcc54f3-216e-40c7-acaf-e9c78656782f'::uuid, 'The software will also look across different providers to determine if another provider was paid for the same procedure, for the same enrollee on the same date of service.', 'extract:denial-rules-2026-08'),
